    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the \"art\" is just suffering. most of the time it's just struggle, anxiety, and pain. if the performance is mostly just agony and it's destined to be forgotten anyway, why is it a \"beauty\"? it feels like we're being forced to endure this misery for no reason. if there's no grander purpose or lasting impact, then isn't the most logical thing to just... stop? to just let the void have its silence?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
